{# The paragraph inside the invoice's "Billed beyond stock" alert. A template rather than a string
   parameter of sales_detail_stock_override_panel.html.twig because it carries its own markup —
   see that partial's `noticeTemplate` note.

   Parameters
   ----------
   count  required  how many lines on this invoice bill past what the region had. #}
<strong>{{ count }} line(s) on this invoice bill more than the region had
available.</strong> That is a decision somebody took, not a mistake the system let through: the
figures below are what they were shown at the time, and the reason is what they gave for going
ahead. Backorder capacity is never cover on an invoice &mdash; an invoice line has no split to
fall back on &mdash; so nothing but stock ever stood behind these units.
